ept of the elliptic cone, we plug $x=0$ and $y=0$ into the equation and solve for $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{0}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{{0}^{2}}{9} & ={z}^{2} \\\\ 0+0 & ={z}^{2} \\\\ {z}^{2} & =0 \\\\ z & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intercept with the $z$-axis is $(0,0,0)$ only." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360474 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186360188 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360474 #edb/ref 1069 "q-94698" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360474 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360474 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the center of the elliptic cone $9(x+3)^{2}+4(y+2)^{2}={z}^{2}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360474 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b8a937fd-a8d7-55e4-aa58-5b69cf851776" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360474 #edb/ref 1074 "The general equation of an elliptic cone with center at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-{x}_{0})^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-{y}_{0})^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=\\frac{(z-{z}_{0})^{2}}{{c}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nTo find the center, we rewrite our equation in standard form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9(x+3)^{2}+4(y+2)^{2} & =(z-0)^{2} \\\\ \\frac{(x+3)^{2}}{1/9}+\\frac{(y+2)^{2}}{1/4} & =(z-0)^{2} \\\\ \\frac{(x-(-3))^{2}}{1/9}+\\frac{(y-(-2))^{2}}{1/4} & =(z-0)^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us the equation of an elliptic cone that has its center at $(-3,-2,0).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381903 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186381904 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381903 #edb/ref 1069 "q-35594" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381903 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381903 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that the intersection of the elliptic cone $\\frac{(x+4)^{2}}{16}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{8}={z}^{2}$ and the plane $z=-1$ is an ellipse, what is the length of its major axis?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381903 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "4e599e36-3b40-5e2d-af38-60f8a4820d9c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381903 #edb/ref 1074 "To find the intersection of the elliptic cone and the plane $z=-1,$ we substitute $z=-1$ into the equation of the elliptic cone, and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x+4)^{2}}{16}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{8} & ={z}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{(x+4)^{2}}{16}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{8} & =(-1)^{2} \\\\ \\frac{(x+4)^{2}}{16}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{8} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x+4)^{2}}{{4}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{(2\\sqrt{2})^{2}} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us the equation of an ellipse with a semi-major axis of length $a=4.$ Therefore, the major axis has length $2a=8.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381904 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186381905 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381904 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186381906 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381904 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186381907 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381904 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186381908 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381904 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186381909 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381904 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381904 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381904 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186381906 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381904 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "5b5b73d9-d33d-503d-b72a-d3c35ccecc6d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381905 #edb/ref 1080 "6\\sqrt{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381905 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381905 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "4c7c7baf-2af7-5778-a178-ee26e7ab310e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381906 #edb/ref 1080 "8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381906 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381906 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "348c2dc5-e846-5787-8fe3-f2f58d451f78" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381907 #edb/ref 1080 "2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381907 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381907 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "84cd3c09-7140-5d22-ab4b-8de0bb1f2245" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381908 #edb/ref 1080 "6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381908 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381908 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "2e7dacb9-bf6b-5580-9907-3dc8fa338664" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381909 #edb/ref 1080 "2\\sqrt{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381909 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381909 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "bbc209e6-8980-5ac6-ad04-17486246efb5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186399275 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186399276 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186399275 #edb/ref 1069 "q-94609" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186399275 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186399275 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the center of the elliptic cone $4(x-1)^{2}+10(y-4)^{2}={z}^{2}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186399275 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "8ed2d339-1669-5c85-b00e-540acdbbec95" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186399275 #edb/ref 1074 "The general equation of an elliptic cone with center at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-{x}_{0})^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-{y}_{0})^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=\\frac{(z-{z}_{0})^{2}}{{c}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nTo find the center, we rewrite our equation in standard form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4(x-1)^{2}+10(y-4)^{2} & =(z-0)^{2} \\\\ \\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{1/4}+\\frac{(y-4)^{2}}{1/10} & =(z-0)^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us the equation of an elliptic cone that has its center at $(1,4,0).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
